SMB Market Intel — Admin CLI Tool
===================================

A simple command-line utility for checking user registrations,
activity, data status, and more — directly from your server terminal.

Prerequisites
-------------
- Docker containers must be running (docker compose up -d)
- Run from the MobileCompetition project directory


Usage
-----
  ./smb-admin.sh <command>


Available Commands
------------------

  users       List all registered users with their signup dates
              and a total count.

  activity    Show each user's activity: how many data refreshes
              and AI analyses they've run, plus when they were
              last active.

  signups     Show new user signups grouped by day — useful for
              tracking growth over time.

  insights    Summary of all AI-generated analyses by type
              (Provider, Market, Comparison, etc.) with counts
              and the most recent generation date.

  requests    List all development requests submitted by users
              through the Dev Requests page, including who
              submitted them and their current status.

  data        Show each provider's offer count and when their
              data was last updated — handy for checking if a
              refresh is needed.

  stats       One-line overview: total users, providers, offers,
              insights, and dev requests.

  help        Show the built-in help message.


Examples
--------

  # Quick health check
  ./smb-admin.sh stats

  # See who signed up today
  ./smb-admin.sh signups

  # Check if anyone is actively using the tool
  ./smb-admin.sh activity

  # See if provider data is stale
  ./smb-admin.sh data

  # Check feature requests from the team
  ./smb-admin.sh requests


Notes
-----
- All queries run against the PostgreSQL container
  (mobilecompetition-db-1) via docker exec.
- No data is modified — every command is read-only.
- If the containers aren't running you'll see a connection error;
  just start them with: docker compose up -d

